      "side": 1,
      "message": "This can actually be changed into a helper function:\n\nint bbram_valid(enum bbram_data_index index, int bytes)\n{\n      \t/* Check index */\n\tif (index \u003c 0 || index + bytes \u003e NPCX_BBRAM_SIZE)\n\t\treturn 0;\n\n\t/* Check BBRAM is valid */\n\tif (IS_BIT_SET(NPCX_BKUP_STS, NPCX_BKUP_STS_IBBR)) {\n\t\tCPRINTF(\"IBBR set: BBRAM corrupted!\\n\");\n\t\treturn 0;\n\t}\n\n        return 1;\n}\n\nand then read/write can just use the return value from validate:\n\nstatic int bbram_data_write(...)\n{\n     ...\n     if (!bbram_valid(..))\n             return EC_ERROR_INVAL;\n     ...\n}\n\nstatic int bbram_data_read(...)\n{\n     ...\n     if (!bbram_valid(...))\n              return 0;\n     ...\n}",
